vLLM #63351 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63351), backported to v0.32.0, on #63350.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.32.0 (5df63a720):

  e873633ac [Core] Priority scheduling: hold lower-priority prefill for first tokens (cherry-picked from dbe86f3d8)
  b703ac4d7 [Core] Priority scheduling: skip the prefix lookup when the cap would hold nothing (cherry-picked from d0102c343)
    Backport: v0.32.0's request queues stay stock, so the queue method
    is the scheduler's _has_lower_priority_than here, with the same answer.
  1104add2b [Core] Priority scheduling: count the budget cap's holds in scheduler stats (cherry-picked from 685fdbcf3)
    Backport: v0.32.0's SchedulerStats and Prometheus logger have no field
    for them, so the scheduler counts them and make_stats leaves them.
  f3768bde2 [Core] Priority scheduling: count a request's first tokens in flight (cherry-picked from 9013ed433)

